    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Periods can now be closed, and all 4 Playwright tests in `bin/e2e` pass.\n\n**Stored data**\n- A new migration, `V15__period_closed.sql`, adds two columns to the `period` table: a `closed` flag and a `closed_total` that holds the due-total fixed at closing.\n\n**Server**\n- **Closing:** `POST /api/sheets/{sheetId}/periods/{id}/close` calculates the period's due-total and saves it. The total is the sum of the dues of the open and settled claims dated in the period, using the same `RollupService.figure` the rollups use. Closing writes `PERIOD_CLOSED sheet=\u2026 by=\u2026 period=<name> total=<due-total>` to the audit file. Closing a period that is already closed is refused.\n- **Refusals:** a claim dated inside a closed period can't be added, edited, opened, settled or voided. An edit is also refused if it would move a claim's date into a closed period. A refused action writes nothing to the store or the audit file.\n- **Locking:** adding and editing a claim now lock the sheet, as status changes already did. This stops a claim from slipping into a period while it is being closed.\n\n**Front end**\n- Each period row now shows `period-closed` (yes/no) and a `period-close` button, and shows `period-error` when closing is refused.\n- Once a period is closed, `period-due-total` shows the stored total, so later rate changes don't alter it. Individual claim dues and the sheet rollups still recalculate, which is what the tests expect.\n- Refused claim actions use the existing claim error elements.\n\nThe test helper also mentions a \"reopen\" action, but the request doesn't ask for it, so I didn't add it.",
